{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>This is the law of the sin-offering</b> — The commandment in the section of Leviticus followed the order: the burnt-offering, the meal-offering, the sacrifice of peace-offerings, the sin-offering, and the guilt-offering, for at first He spoke of freewill offerings and afterward of obligatory offerings for sin. But here the explanation was for the burnt-offering and the meal-offering, and afterward for the sin-offering and the guilt-offering, for He wished to explain the laws of kodshei kodashim (most holy offerings), since one rule applies to all of them, as He said concerning the meal-offering (Leviticus 6:10): \"It is most holy, like the sin-offering and like the guilt-offering,\" and afterward He will explain the law of kodashim kalim (lesser holy offerings). \n\nNow He introduces many new things in this section: \"This is the law of the sin-offering\" — one law for all sin-offerings, that even the inner sin-offerings whose blood was sprinkled require washing of garments; one might think even the bird sin-offering, therefore Scripture says \"this.\" And He said: \"In the place where the burnt-offering is slaughtered shall the sin-offering be slaughtered before YHWH\" — that all sin-offerings may be slaughtered only in the north (v. 18), since this was not stated in the section of Leviticus except for the sin-offering of the anointed priest (4:24) and the individual (4:29), but here all are included — the sin-offerings of the congregation and the inner sin-offerings. \n\nThey further derived (Torat Kohanim, parashah 3:2): \"Most holy\" — to include the communal peace-offerings, that they too may be slaughtered only in the north, because in all kodshei kodashim the north was required. \"It is\" — this excludes the thanksgiving-offering and the ram of the nazirite. \n\nAnd He now also gives the flesh of the sin-offerings to the sons of Aaron (Leviticus 6:22), and He commanded that it be eaten in the court of the Tent of Meeting (Leviticus 6:19) — the males among them and not the daughters of Aaron — and He introduced many laws concerning that which is absorbed from the sin-offering (Leviticus 6:20–21)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The verse citations embedded mid-sentence (e.g., 'שם מ'ח') appear to refer back to Leviticus 6:18 and its vicinity; rendered as (v. 18) etc."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:01.826437703Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}